# Run LLMs locally: Llama 3, Mistral, Gemma, DeepSeek-R1, ...
# NOTE: a high-end AMD or NVidia GPU is required. See docs in
# https://github.com/ollama/ollama, https://itsfoss.com/ollama/
# and https://itsfoss.com/install-deepseek-r1-locally-linux/
#
# Ellama has been removed because it doesn't work properly with
# latest models. It's highly recommended to use Open WebUI; the
# best way to run it is with Docker or Podman. I prefere Podman
# in rootless mode, so I created a Open WebUI container with:
#
#    podman run -d --network=host \
#      --cpus=2 \
#      --memory=1g \
#      -e WEBUI_AUTH=False \
#      -e OLLAMA_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:11434 \
#      -e OFFLINE_MODE=true \
#      -e HF_HUB_OFFLINE=1 \
#      -e HF_HUB_DISABLE_TELEMETRY=1 \
#      -e RAG_EMBEDDING_ENGINE=ollama \
#      -e RAG_EMBEDDING_MODEL=bge-m3 \
#      -v open-webui:/app/backend/data \
#      --name open-webui \
#      --restart always \
#      ghcr.io/open-webui/open-webui:main
#
# With the above configuration, Open WebUI simply acts as an offline
# interface to Ollama (all connections to Hugginface and telemetry are
# disabled). For document vectorization, I use the multilingual embedded
# model "bge-m3"; if only English is needed, use "nomic-embed" (lighter).
# See /etc/portage/package.use/01-local-hw.use for required use flags.
dev-python/ollama::local
acct-group/ollama::local
acct-user/ollama::local
sci-ml/ggml::local
sci-ml/ollama::local

